# e5m3 E1 "e5m3_wickmoor" (docs/design/mission-e5-03.md, Cinematic hooks; script-episodes-4-8/e5m3.md 1): 12 s at 0:00,
# mode=pause over the live mission (the spec's HOLD runs as PAUSE). Wickmoor (90 x 90, the churchyard inside +-42): the
# Lantern House with its bell tower at (0, 0), the porch lamps (-5, 8) / (5, 8), the street lamps, the gravedigger's hut
# (-32, 32), Malrik's start (-28, 28) with Soot and Bramble at his sides.
# 1) CRANE down the bell tower to the lamps and the patrols' lantern pools: L1; 2) LOW on the hut yard: the boy with the
# candle, two dogs at his heels (orbits the live hero, tag `malrik`; the cast stands at the start for cine's checks).
# Axis: every camera stays EAST of the boy (the ep3_opening rule for Malrik's scenes). Fallback: the end state says
# L1-L4 and shows the candle hint.
cine e5m3_wickmoor  title="Wickmoor"  mode=pause  letterbox=2.39  seed=531  length=11..13
env night  moon_yaw=200  moon_pitch=-30  energy=0.35
cast  malrik    res://art/units/wizards/malrik.tscn  at=(-28, 0, 28)  yaw=200
cast  narrator  capsule  at=(0, 0, -300)  hidden=1

# CRANE down the bell tower past the moon to the lamps and the lantern pools
shot W1 6.5  cam=crane  from=(6, 24, -6)  to=(8, 9, 4)  look=(0, 20, -1)>(-6, 1, 10)  fov=50>46  in=fade_black:0.6
  at 0.0  sfx res://assets/audio/forge/sfx/evenmead_amb.wav  vol=-14
  at 0.4  line narrator "Wickmoor buried its dead with their rings on. Lately, someone had been taking them back."
# LOW on the hut yard: the boy with the candle, the two dogs at his heels
shot W2 5.5  cam=orbit  pivot=malrik  r=3.8  h=0.8  deg=-20>-8
  at 0.3  sfx res://assets/audio/forge/sfx/snow_step.wav  vol=-18
  at 4.9  fade alpha=1 time=0.6